Gleem OBS Runtime — third-party notices
=======================================

This image is an aggregation of separately licensed programs. Nothing here is
statically linked into anything else: OBS, GStreamer and Selkies are separate
processes started by runtime-init, which is Gleem's own code.

Where the licences are
----------------------

Every Debian package in this image carries its own licence at
/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright — 573 of them at the time of writing,
including obs-studio. `dpkg-query -W` lists what is installed.

Two payloads are not Debian packages and are therefore called out here:

  /opt/selkies       Selkies, MPL-2.0     licence at /usr/share/doc/selkies/LICENSE
  /opt/selkies-web   Selkies, MPL-2.0     licence at /opt/selkies-web/LICENSE

Within the web bundle, lib/guacamole-keyboard-selkies.js is Apache-2.0 from
Apache Guacamole and carries its own header and an upstream modification note.

Obtaining source
----------------

Every GPL- and LGPL-licensed component in this image is an **unmodified binary
package from Debian trixie**. Gleem has patched none of them. Their complete
corresponding source is published by Debian and can be fetched for any package
in this image with:

    apt-get source <package>

against the Debian trixie archive, or browsed at https://sources.debian.org/.

For anyone who cannot use that route, Gleem will provide the complete
corresponding source for any GPL- or LGPL-licensed component of this image on
request, for no more than the cost of distribution, for three years from the
date this image was distributed. Contact: hello@ghostzero.de.

